 "slug": "tamagoyaki",
 "sources": [],
 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Beat the eggs with the seasonings until the sugar dissolves:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\">1 tbsp</span></li><li>sake <span class=\"amt\">1 tsp</span></li><li>brown sugar <span class=\"amt\">2 tsp</span></li><li>salt <span class=\"amt\">a pinch</span></li><li>dashi <span class=\"amt\">1–2 tbsp</span></li></ul></li><li>Cut through the whites with chopsticks rather than whipping — you don’t want foam.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Mix",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Press the chopsticks to the bottom of the bowl and cut side to side through the whites — don't whip.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/1-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/1.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "3 min",
   "title": "Mix",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "3",
     "name_html": "Eggs"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Heat the pan on medium-low and wipe a thin film of oil over it with a folded paper towel.</li><li>A drop of egg should sizzle gently, not spit.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Heat and oil the pan",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/2.webp",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "2 min",
   "title": "Heat and oil the pan",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "a little",
     "name_html": "Neutral oil"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Pour in about a quarter of the egg and tilt to cover the pan.</li><li>Pop any big bubbles.</li><li>When the bottom is set but the top is still a little wet, roll it from the far end towards you.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "First layer",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Pour in about a quarter of the egg and tilt the pan so it covers the bottom thinly.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/3-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "When the bottom has set but the top is still a little wet, roll it from the far end towards you.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/3-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~1 min",
   "title": "First layer",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Push the roll back to the far end and wipe oil over the empty part of the pan.</p>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Push back and re-oil",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Push the roll to the far end and wipe oil over the empty part.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/4-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": null,
   "title": "Push back and re-oil",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Pour in the next quarter and lift the roll so egg runs underneath it.</li><li>Sprinkle the <b>nori flakes</b> over this layer, then roll towards you again.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Second layer, with nori",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Pour in the next quarter, then lift the roll with chopsticks and tilt the pan so the raw egg runs underneath it — that's what glues the layers together.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/5-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Once the bottom has just set, sprinkle the nori flakes over the new layer, then roll towards you.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/5-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/5.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~1 min",
   "title": "Second layer, with nori",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "1–2 tsp",
     "name_html": "Green nori flakes"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Push, oil and pour with the rest of the egg — usually one or two more layers.</li><li>Each time, <b>lift the roll so the new egg runs underneath it</b> before rolling — that’s what glues the layers together.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Repeat",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Every layer: push, oil, pour, then lift the roll so the egg runs underneath before rolling.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/6-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/6.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "2–3 min",
   "title": "Repeat",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Tip the roll onto a bamboo mat (or a paper towel), wrap it and press gently into a neat block.</li><li>Leave it for 5 minutes to set.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Shape and rest",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Tip the roll onto a bamboo mat, wrap it and press gently into a neat block.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/7-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/7.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "title": "Shape and rest",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Cut into 2 cm slices — the nori shows as a green swirl.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Slice",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cut into 2 cm slices with a sharp knife, steadying the block with a claw grip.",
      "src": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/8-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tamagoyaki/8.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": null,
   "title": "Slice",
